WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.586 --> 00:00:17.088
Hood knew that the sheriff had vowed to catch him.

2
00:00:17.808 --> 00:00:22.431
So for almost a year, he and his men did not leave Sherwood Forest.

3
00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:32.336
They stayed deep in the woods, amusing themselves with archery games and wrestling matches.

4
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.643
But at last Robin grew restless and bored.

5
00:00:44.006 --> 00:00:47.129
off to find some adventure," he announced one day.

6
00:00:52.713 --> 00:00:57.977
Walking along the road, he soon met a young butcher driving a cart filled with meat.

7
00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:02.360
The day was sunny and the butcher was whistling a happy tune.

8
00:01:04.992 --> 00:01:05.773
"Good morning!"

9
00:01:06.113 --> 00:01:06.834
called Robin.

10
00:01:06.854 --> 00:01:09.155
"You seem cheerful today."

11
00:01:09.175 --> 00:01:11.097
"I am cheerful!"

12
00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:12.137
said the butcher.

13
00:01:12.157 --> 00:01:15.720
"Next week I'm marrying the prettiest girl in Locksley!"

14
00:01:17.561 --> 00:01:20.663
"Oh, I know Locksley well," said Robin.

15
00:01:20.683 --> 00:01:22.505
"I used to live there."

16
00:01:22.525 --> 00:01:23.706
"You did?

17
00:01:24.306 --> 00:01:24.966
What's your name?"

18
00:01:24.987 --> 00:01:26.828
"Robin Hood."

19
00:01:26.848 --> 00:01:28.909
"The famous outlaw!"

20
00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:30.570
gasped the butcher.

21
00:01:30.591 --> 00:01:31.451
"Oh no!

22
00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.372
Please don't rob me!"

23
00:01:33.572 --> 00:01:36.114
"I won't rob an honest young man from Locksley!

24
00:01:36.714 --> 00:01:40.317
Especially one who's getting married next week."

25
00:01:40.337 --> 00:01:43.079
Robin laughed as he looked over the man's cart and horse.

26
00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:46.781
"Where are you going with all this meat?"

27
00:01:48.102 --> 00:01:52.325
"I'm going to the market in Nottingham to sell my beef and mutton," the butcher replied.

28
00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:56.528
"I'd like to be a butcher for a day," Robin Hood said.

29
00:01:56.548 --> 00:01:58.789
"How much is all this meat worth?"

30
00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.512
The man named a price, and Robin took out his money.

31
00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.341
"Here, I'll give you double that amount."

32
00:02:08.103 --> 00:02:13.106
"Sold!" The young man climbed down from the cart and handed Robin the horse's reins.

33
00:02:13.126 --> 00:02:15.927
"Thank you, Robin Hood," he said.

34
00:02:15.947 --> 00:02:17.889
"You're not a thief after all.

35
00:02:18.609 --> 00:02:20.310
You're an honest and generous man."

36
00:02:21.591 --> 00:02:24.332
Robin smiled at the joyful young butcher.

37
00:02:24.352 --> 00:02:26.233
"It's my pleasure.

38
00:02:26.814 --> 00:02:29.495
Now get back to Locksley and your pretty girl."

39
00:02:34.984 --> 00:02:38.407
Robin rode into Nottingham and soon found the market.

40
00:02:39.047 --> 00:02:42.529
He set up a stall near the other butchers and spread out the meat.

41
00:02:42.549 --> 00:02:44.691
"Good housewives!"

42
00:02:45.011 --> 00:02:45.572
he called.

43
00:02:45.592 --> 00:02:48.654
"I'll sell you three pennies' worth of meat for one penny.

44
00:02:49.054 --> 00:02:50.075
Widows and poor women!

45
00:02:50.395 --> 00:02:51.656
I'll give you your meat for free.

46
00:02:52.236 --> 00:02:54.298
Who wants to buy something from me?"

47
00:02:55.398 --> 00:02:58.140
People began to crowd around Robin's stall.

48
00:02:59.221 --> 00:03:02.924
His prices were so low that no one visited the other butchers.

49
00:03:04.112 --> 00:03:07.274
The other butchers began to talk and grumble among themselves.

50
00:03:07.294 --> 00:03:10.456
"Where did that guy come from?"

51
00:03:10.476 --> 00:03:13.839
"He must have stolen the meat and cart!"

52
00:03:14.079 --> 00:03:15.220
complained one butcher.

53
00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.122
"No," said another butcher.

54
00:03:18.142 --> 00:03:21.324
"A thief would never sell the meat so cheaply.

55
00:03:22.024 --> 00:03:24.246
He'd want to make as much money as possible."

56
00:03:24.266 --> 00:03:28.989
"I think he's the son of a rich man," said a third butcher.

57
00:03:29.009 --> 00:03:33.472
"He's trying to sell as many of his father's things as he can."

58
00:03:34.144 --> 00:03:36.266
The other butchers nodded in agreement.

59
00:03:37.847 --> 00:03:40.710
It didn't take long for Robin to sell all the meat.

60
00:03:41.731 --> 00:03:43.972
The third butcher went over to talk to him.

61
00:03:43.993 --> 00:03:45.534
"Good day!"

62
00:03:45.814 --> 00:03:46.475
said the butcher.

63
00:03:46.495 --> 00:03:53.200
"The Sheriff of Nottingham has invited all the butchers to a feast at the banquet hall.

64
00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:54.521
Come join us!"

65
00:03:54.541 --> 00:03:58.645
"Gladly!" Robin said merrily.

66
00:03:59.165 --> 00:04:01.848
He was packing a lot of adventure into this day.

67
00:04:03.108 --> 00:04:05.350
The sheriff was already at the banquet hall.

68
00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:10.233
The other butchers told him about the rich young man selling meat.

69
00:04:10.873 --> 00:04:15.697
"Perhaps I can take advantage of this wealthy fool," the sheriff said to himself.

70
00:04:16.517 --> 00:04:19.739
When the new butcher arrived, the sheriff waved him over.

71
00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.681
"Please. Sit next to me."

72
00:04:25.543 --> 00:04:28.445
The two men joked and laughed throughout the meal.

73
00:04:29.206 --> 00:04:32.608
The sheriff never realized he was talking to Robin Hood.

74
00:04:34.848 --> 00:04:36.469
"You're quite amusing!"

75
00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:37.930
said the sheriff.

76
00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:42.013
"I know you like to be entertained," said Robin slyly.

77
00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:46.856
"Wasn't it fun when Robin Hood won your gold arrow at the archery contest?"

78
00:04:47.537 --> 00:04:51.639
The sheriff's face suddenly got dark, and the room went silent.

79
00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:55.502
A couple of butchers turned away, to hide their grins.

80
00:04:55.522 --> 00:04:58.824
"It's time for a toast!"

81
00:04:59.585 --> 00:05:00.966
Robin raised his cup.

82
00:05:01.526 --> 00:05:02.447
"To the sheriff!

83
00:05:03.027 --> 00:05:04.348
May you catch Robin Hood!

84
00:05:05.012 --> 00:05:07.053
And may everyone enjoy this feast.

85
00:05:07.713 --> 00:05:09.214
I'm going to pay for it!"

86
00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:12.915
The sheriff laughed, though not quite as loudly as before.

87
00:05:12.935 --> 00:05:16.557
"Young butcher, you spend your money so freely.

88
00:05:17.157 --> 00:05:19.758
You must own a lot of land and animals."

89
00:05:19.778 --> 00:05:24.860
"I don't know how much land we have," Robin said with a shrug.

90
00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.781
"But it is a lot.

91
00:05:27.482 --> 00:05:30.923
And my family has more than five hundred horned animals.

92
00:05:31.563 --> 00:05:32.924
We haven't been able to sell them.

93
00:05:33.512 --> 00:05:35.454
So that's why I became a butcher."

94
00:05:36.695 --> 00:05:40.519
By now the sheriff was certain he could trick this silly butcher.

95
00:05:41.239 --> 00:05:43.201
He also knew he could make some money.

96
00:05:43.942 --> 00:05:45.844
The sheriff smiled at Robin Hood.

97
00:05:45.864 --> 00:05:49.807
"I like you very much," he said slyly.

98
00:05:49.828 --> 00:05:52.590
"You're a generous man and very entertaining.

99
00:05:53.031 --> 00:05:54.272
Perhaps I can help you."
